<title>SINGAPORE: Courts Singapore proposes bonus issue.</title>
<headline>Courts Singapore proposes bonus issue.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Furniture retailer Courts (Singapore) Ltd said on Friday it was proposing a one for two bonus issue.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement the issue would lead to the creation of 53.63 million new Courts shares.</p>
<p>The purpose of the issue was to increase the capital base of the company and to reward members for their continued support, it added.</p>
<p>Courts reported a 2.43 percent rise in net profit for the year ended March 31, 1997 to Singapore $13.37 million.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
